= Introduction

Ball possession is one of the most widely used descriptors in football, but tracking providers do not report it directly. It has to be inferred from where 22 players and the ball are. The More than a Hack 2027 benchmark @mtah2027 frames this as frame-level labelling of one full LaLiga match, FC Barcelona (H) vs Athletic Club (A): 199,319 frames at 25 fps, of which 158,857 are graded. The inputs are automatic and uncorrected. Tracks fragment and swap identities, carry no player identifiers, and the ball is missing on about 41% of graded frames @mtah2027.

Two properties of the benchmark shape our design. First, the ranking metric is *spellF1*, not per-frame accuracy. A possession ("spell") is a maximal run of one team with the ball alive. Predicted and true spells are matched one-to-one at IoU thresholds ${0.3, ..., 0.7}$ and the F1 is averaged across those thresholds. Every spell counts once, so a single flicker inside a long possession costs a whole spell, and a missed 2-s possession costs as much as a missed 40-s one. Second, the public ground truth (GT) covers only 5 minutes and 17 possessions. That is enough to check the pipeline but far too little to select a model. All selection therefore used external data, and the public score is reported only as a post-freeze diagnostic.

Our contributions are: (i) an exploratory analysis of the target tracking that motivates a segmentation-first design (@sec:eda); (ii) a short-spell-weighted TCN ensemble with rate-calibrated Viterbi decoding (@sec:method); (iii) a pre-registered, provider-balanced selection protocol over 96 configurations (@sec:protocol); (iv) a full account of the results, including the negative ones, and a from-scratch reproduction (@sec:results); and (v) an explainability study of the submitted model (@sec:xai).

= Data and Exploratory Analysis <sec:eda>

== Target match

The *tactical* recording is the evaluation timeline. Row $i$ of a submission is frame $i$ of this video. The automatic tracking (ATD) contains 46 track slots (24 home, 22 away), more than twice the number of players on the pitch. Table I lists the main statistics, computed on the ATD and Smart Tagging without using the GT.

