== Competition public window (diagnostic)

We re-scored the submitted CSV with the official scorer; it reproduces the recorded public result exactly (Table III). The method improves on every official baseline under spellF1 and also under macroF1, Cohen's $kappa$ and transition F1. It predicts #w5.poss possessions against 17 in the GT: #N.public_transitions.matched GT transitions are matched, #N.public_transitions.missed are missed and #N.public_transitions.spurious are spurious. @fig:timeline shows the cause. The long possessions are recovered with boundaries within a few frames, but several brief Barcelona/Athletic exchanges between minutes 10 and 12 are absorbed into longer spells. The same pattern appears in the confusion matrix (@fig:confusion): live-ball team errors are rare (#pct(cm.at(0).at(1) / cm.at(0).sum()) of H frames, #pct(cm.at(1).at(0) / cm.at(1).sum()) of A frames), while #pct((cm.at(2).at(0) + cm.at(2).at(1)) / cm.at(2).sum()) of dead-ball frames are labelled live. That is consistent with dead stretches being detected late or shortened.

