) <tab:ablation>

*Which inputs matter.* Integrated Gradients @sundararajan2017ig (64 steps, 16 crops of 512 samples, three seeds; median completeness error 0.9%) attribute 41.6% / 49.6% of the dead-ball / team logit to the 23 team-shape channels, 39.7% / 35.9% to the player set, 16.7% / 12.6% to the ball channels and 2.0% to the validity flag (@fig:ig). The players' attacking velocity is the strongest single input for both heads; the dead-ball head also relies on ball speed and player speed, since play stops when motion stops. Occluding each group over the whole match and rerunning the full pipeline confirms the ranking (Table V). Without team shape the output fragments (395 possessions) and public spellF1 falls to 0.484; without the player set possessions merge (238). Without the ball channels only 4.0% of labels change, mostly through the dead-ball head. This is why the method keeps working when the ball is missing.

