  placement: top,
) <fig:attn>

*Where the seeds disagree.* On average, the spread of P(home) across seeds is the same near decoded changes and elsewhere (sd 0.033 vs. 0.032); its peaks (up to 0.13, @fig:seeds) fall on the contested exchanges between minutes 10 and 12 that are analysed below. The spread of P(dead), by contrast, is 4.3× higher within ±2 s of a decoded change than elsewhere (sd 0.038 vs. 0.009; not plotted). Model uncertainty is concentrated on stoppages and on brief contested exchanges.

