*Error anatomy.* On the public window, 11 of 17 GT possessions are recovered at IoU 0.5; recovered possessions last 17.8 s on average and missed ones 7.5 s. The misses cluster between minutes 9.9 and 11.6: three short Barcelona touches (0.8, 1.3 and 3.5 s) inside Athletic possessions, and the Athletic spells they split. The ball is visible throughout and P(home) stays at 0.09–0.46, so the failure is brief contested exchanges, not ball loss (@fig:errors). These misses are systematic rather than random: on the two shortest touches (0.8 and 1.3 s) the mean P(home) is 0.16 and 0.09 with a seed standard deviation of at most 0.05, so all seeds agree that Athletic has the ball and a larger ensemble would not recover them. Only the 3.5-s touch is borderline (P(home) 0.46, seed sd 0.08, the largest of any GT possession). Long recovered possessions (> 10 s) have P(home) above 0.95 or below 0.07 with seed sd at most 0.02. Every GT possession shorter than 2 s is missed, consistent with the 1-s merge and the ±2 s effective context: a sub-second touch cannot outweigh the evidence around it.

